IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `priv51-nouns`

-- Row il-51. THE CITATIONS, as typed values, and the per-person rates.
-- A citation is encoded as TWO descriptions: what the citing words say they point at, and what the target is. A test compares them. Where they differ, the citation does not point at what it says;
-- that is a defect, kept in an expected-red file with its count declared in check.sh and encoding.json.
-- Nine citation defects are recorded with seven sound controls (P3(a) and P3(b) share one, as do P8(a) and P8(b)), and one rounding question about per-person rates (P6).
-- LIMBS. Limb (a) is the question whether the target is as the citing words say; limb (b) is the question whether the citing words still read so in the latest official text of the citing provision.
-- Each limb says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in priv51-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource text is not official, and neither is the non-official archive (olaw.org.il) the 2004 regulations were fetched from.
-- A date for which the sources held give no answer is NOTHING; there is no REFUSE.
-- The Hebrew on the official-instrument lines was typed from page images; the pages are deposited as images in registers/source-bundle. That Hebrew is not machine-checked against the images, and the Kovetz HaTakanot and Yalkut HaPirsumim pages are not checked against any text layer.
--
-- THE DAY THE AMENDMENT TOOK EFFECT. Amendment 13 was published on 14.8.2024, which the page footer prints with its Hebrew date (10 Av 5784; the calendar routine reproduced 30 Kislev 5785 = 31 December 2024 first, and 10 Av 5784 = 14 August 2024).
-- Its section 74(א) says it takes effect "one year from the day of its publication". Whether that is 14 or 15 August 2025 depends on how the days of a period are counted, which was not looked up (fork D0 in NOTES.md).
-- This row sets the LATER day, 15 August 2025, wherever the answer is a day the cited text stopped being the text in force, so that the row says no more than that the text has stopped by then; for 14 August 2025 and before, it says NOTHING.
-- ext:[SH 3287 p.1430, read from the page image] | ספר החוקים 3287, י' באב התשפ"ד, 14.8.2024
-- ext:[SH 3287 p.1495, read from the page image] | (א) תחילתו של חוק זה שנה מיום פרסומו (להלן – יום התחילה).

§ `Cross-references`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation points at what it says` MEANS c's `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS c's `the target is`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs were read from the official instruments` MEANS
    c's `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    AND c's `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

-- Whether the text the citing words name is the text in force on a day. The only answer the sources held give is the day it stopped being in force and the days from then on; for any earlier day,
-- and for a citation with no recorded end, the answer is NOTHING (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the named text is in force on` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on`
        WHEN JUST stopped THEN IF day AT LEAST stopped THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The documented fork of the Interpretation Law section 25: what the citing words reach when read through that section. NOTHING where this row does not say.
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a provision is about`
`the reading through the Interpretation Law section 25 reaches` MEANS
    c's `read through the Interpretation Law section 25 the citing words reach`

