§ `Per-person rates and the rounding rule`

-- P6. Section 23לב(ב) says the amounts in section 23כו and in the Third, Fourth and Fifth Schedules are updated each 1 January and that "the said amount shall be rounded to the nearest multiple of 10 new shekels"; the first update is in 2026.
-- The rates the consolidation prints as enacted for the first rate of each of section 23כו(ג), (ד) and (ה) are 50, 2 and 4 shekels (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY). Of the rates the notice updates, 50 and 100 are multiples of ten, and 2, 4 and 8 are not.
-- The notice of 7.10.2026 (Yalkut HaPirsumim 15000, p. 654, read from a crop of the page image; the calendar routine gives 26 Tishrei 5787 = 7 October 2026) prints 51.18 for 50, 102.36 for 100, 2.05 for 2, 4.09 for 4 and 8.19 for 8; none of those printed rates is a multiple of ten.
-- ext:[YP 15000 p.654, read from the page image] | ילקוט הפרסומים 15000, כ"ו בתשרי התשפ"ז, 7.10.2026
-- Its footnotes say: "the rounding is done on the final amount of the financial sanction, obtained after the multiplication under the Law".
-- READING A (the literal words of section 23לב(ב)): the updated rate itself is rounded to a multiple of ten shekels. READING B (the notice): the final sanction is rounded. The row does not rule; it records that the printed rates are not what reading A gives.
